cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "FlashProve-Next: Verifiable Inference for Production LLM APIs"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/s-JoL/FlashProve-Next"
url: "https://s-jol.github.io/FlashProve-Next/"
authors:
  - family-names: Song
    given-names: Liang
    email: sl12160010@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  Verifiable inference proofs for closed-weight LLM APIs served in native floating point
  (bf16/fp8/mxfp4, random sampling, FlashAttention, CUDA Graphs, continuous batching, prefix
  caching) while hiding model weights, hidden system prompts, hidden chain of thought, intermediate
  activations, and multi-turn state. Version 1.0.0 includes eleven specifications (specs/01-11),
  28 Lean 4.29.1 modules (696 axiom-audited declarations, zero sorry, standard axioms only), a
  zero-dependency Rust FPN2 verifier (fpn-core / fpn-verify) and detached Python reference, a
  zero-Phase-2 folded ZK-Basefold + FracLogUp-GKR backend evaluated on unsliced Qwen3-0.6B,
  Qwen3-4B, and live vLLM 0.33 Qwen3-30B-A3B-FP8, and offline laptop CPU verification demos.
keywords:
  - verifiable inference
  - zero-knowledge proofs
  - LLM serving
  - cryptography
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
